{"paper": "RRB-Technician-Grade-III-CBT-1-06-Mar-2026-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "answer-anchored", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "3523", "options": [{"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "-1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": "1"}, {"n": 2, "text": "When one-third of a number is increased by 37, the result is 51. Find the sum of the digits of the original number.", "options": [{"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "9", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "digit-sum-and-place-value", "key_answer": "6"}, {"n": 3, "text": "Anisha borrowed ₹28,260 from her friend at 9% per annum, simple interest. She returned the amount after 9 months. How much interest did she pay?7186", "options": [{"text": "₹ 1933.25", "added": false}, {"text": "₹ 1948.20", "added": false}, {"text": "₹ 1907.55", "added": false}, {"text": "₹ 1970.75", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": "1907.55"}, {"n": 4, "text": "The lengths of two trains starting from stations P and Q are in the ratio 3 : 2. When they run in opposite directions at speeds of 54 km/h and 72 km/h, respectively, they cross each other in 30 seconds. The train starting from P crosses a bridge in 90 seconds. Find the length of the bridge.", "options": [{"text": "720 meters", "added": false}, {"text": "740 meters", "added": false}, {"text": "620 meters", "added": false}, {"text": "780 meters", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "two-trains", "key_answer": "720 meters"}, {"n": 5, "text": "A person X invests ₹12,000 for 12 months and person Y invests ₹18,000 but withdraws his investment after 6 months. If the total profit earned on their investment is ₹25,200, what is X’s share in the profit?", "options": [{"text": "₹16,800", "added": false}, {"text": "₹15,700", "added": false}, {"text": "₹14,400", "added": false}, {"text": "₹13,900", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "partnership", "key_answer": "14400"}, {"n": 6, "text": "A cylindrical printing drum of length 2.1 m makes 350 complete revolutions and prints 4158 m² of fabric. What is the radius of the drum? (Take π = 22/7)", "options": [{"text": "60 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "70 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "90 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "80 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": "90 cm"}, {"n": 7, "text": "If a book costs ₹300 and its price is increased by 5%, by how much the new price of the book after the increase is more than the original price?", "options": [{"text": "₹15", "added": false}, {"text": "₹10", "added": false}, {"text": "₹20", "added": false}, {"text": "₹25", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": "15"}, {"n": 8, "text": "One pipe can fill the tank in 20 min, while another pipe can empty the completely filled tank in 45 min. If both the pipes are operated together on empty tank, how long (in min) will it take to fill one-fourth of the tank?3940", "options": [{"text": "36", "added": false}, {"text": "27", "added": false}, {"text": "9", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Pipes-Cisterns", "sub": "combined-pipes", "key_answer": "9"}, {"n": 9, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "38", "added": false}, {"text": "46", "added": false}, {"text": "42", "added": false}, {"text": "52", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": "46"}, {"n": 10, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "254", "added": false}, {"text": "260", "added": false}, {"text": "258", "added": false}, {"text": "252", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "expression-values", "key_answer": "254"}, {"n": 11, "text": "A student scored 84% of the maximum marks in an exam and passed by 62 marks. But when he scored 45% of the marks in the same exam, he failed by 35.5 marks. Find the maximum marks of the exam.", "options": [{"text": "240", "added": false}, {"text": "265", "added": false}, {"text": "250", "added": false}, {"text": "225", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": "250"}, {"n": 12, "text": "3523", "options": [{"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "-1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "factors-divisors", "key_answer": "p^2 for prime p"}, {"n": 13, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "312", "added": false}, {"text": "311", "added": false}, {"text": "322", "added": false}, {"text": "302", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "surds-and-indices", "key_answer": "322"}, {"n": 14, "text": "The average age of a husband and wife at the time of their marriage was 28 years. Their daughter was born two years after their marriage. If the present average age of all three family members is 24 years, how many years ago from now, did the couple get married?", "options": [{"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "7", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ages", "sub": "average-age", "key_answer": "6"}, {"n": 15, "text": "The area of a square is 9 cm2. Its perimeter is equal to the perimeter of a regular hexagon. What is the area (in cm2) of the hexagon? Ans A) 32 D) 40 B) C) Correct Answer: B", "options": [{"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "5.4", "added": true}, {"text": "6.6", "added": true}, {"text": "7", "added": true}], "options_source": "added", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": "6√3"}, {"n": 16, "text": "3158", "options": [{"text": "(iv)", "added": false}, {"text": "(iii)", "added": false}, {"text": "(i)", "added": false}, {"text": "(ii)", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "triangles", "key_answer": "(ii)"}, {"n": 17, "text": "When one-third of a number is increased by 37, the result is 51. Find the sum of the digits of the original number.", "options": [{"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "9", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": "3"}, {"n": 18, "text": "What sum of money (in ₹) will yield ₹720 as simple interest in 2 years at 5% per annum?", "options": [{"text": "7600", "added": false}, {"text": "7200", "added": false}, {"text": "6700", "added": false}, {"text": "7400", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": "7200"}, {"n": 19, "text": "What is the mode of the following data? 51, 48, 50, 55, 44, 52, 45, 52, 44, 49, 55, 54, 44, 54, 43, 45, 55, 47", "options": [{"text": "55", "added": false}, {"text": "54", "added": false}, {"text": "44", "added": false}, {"text": "45", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Elementary Statistics", "sub": "mean-median-mode", "key_answer": "55"}, {"n": 20, "text": "Three workers A, B, C can finish a job in 10, 15, and 20 hours respectively. A and B start; after 2 hours, C joins and they finish the remaining work in t more hours. What is the value of t? (Rounded off to the nearest integer.)", "options": [{"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": "5/3"}, {"n": 21, "text": "What is the mode of the following data? 51, 48, 50, 55, 44, 52, 45, 52, 44, 49, 55, 54, 44, 54, 43, 45, 55, 47", "options": [{"text": "55", "added": false}, {"text": "54", "added": false}, {"text": "44", "added": false}, {"text": "45", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ages", "sub": "present-age", "key_answer": "18"}, {"n": 22, "text": "Anusha starts a business with ₹55,000 and after 7 months, Minal joins Anusha as her partner. After a year, the profit is divided in the ratio 8 : 3. What is Minal's contribution in the capital?", "options": [{"text": "₹50,755", "added": false}, {"text": "₹49,410", "added": false}, {"text": "₹49,500", "added": false}, {"text": "₹48,745", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "partnership", "key_answer": "49500"}, {"n": 23, "text": "A shopkeeper sold a book at a loss of 6%. If the selling price had been increased by ₹960, there would have been a gain of 19%. What was the cost price (in ₹) of the book? 1765", "options": [{"text": "3850", "added": false}, {"text": "3835", "added": false}, {"text": "3840", "added": false}, {"text": "3845", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "successive-transactions", "key_answer": "3840"}, {"n": 24, "text": "Two numbers are in the ratio of 4 : 5, and their HCF is 16. Find the LCM of the two numbers.", "options": [{"text": "360", "added": false}, {"text": "380", "added": false}, {"text": "340", "added": false}, {"text": "320", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": "320"}, {"n": 25, "text": "A dealer buys two articles X and Y for ₹1,300 each. He marks each of them at the same price. He sells X by giving two successive discounts of 84% and 25% and still earns ₹734 as profit. If he sells Y at a single discount of 87%, then what is the profit percentage on Y?", "options": [{"text": "69%", "added": false}, {"text": "68.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "68%", "added": false}, {"text": "69.5%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": "69.5%"}]}